+// n18 ARC-COVERAGE GATE. Restated from ScanRuler's cylinder gates (AGPL: mechanism
+// and constant only, no code): a patch spanning less than ~30 degrees of arc is
+// barely curved over that span, so its radius and axis position are guesses. Its
+// stated reason for defining coverage as 360 - (widest angular gap), rather than by
+// counting occupied bins, is that the former does not shrink just because the mesh
+// is coarse -- which is why this does NOT punish a coarsely tessellated bore.
+//
+// A region already carries its span as [uMin, uMax], so the measurement is free.
+// Target: L10_cross_slide ships 11 cylinders against a truth of 4 faces at R=2.0,
+// seven of them at R=7.2539 -- one curved wall sliced into narrow strips. Env-gated;
+// off => no-op. closed360 regions are exempt by definition (they span 2*pi).
+// n21 TESSELLATION-QUALITY GATE. n18 asks how much arc a patch covers; nothing asked
+// how well that arc is drawn. A cylinder region carries its MEASURED chord sagitta, and
+// refit_build.cpp:365 turns that sagitta into the region's edge tolerance -- honestly,
+// because the mesh really is that coarse. The damage is that the tolerance is then
+// shared with the region's neighbours.
+//
+// Measured on mechparts/15: rid=13 is a 2-triangle, 4-sided patch at R=10, i.e. a 90 deg
+// arc drawn with two facets. Its sagitta is 10*(1-cos45) = 2.928932 mm, so OCCT is
+// licensed to identify points 2.93 mm apart on a part whose real bores are R~8 mm. The
+// faces go invalid (culprit rid=13 src=face faceValid=0), the U0 cascade explodes it and
+// its neighbours, and rid=9/10/11/12 -- four 144-sided bands fitting the mesh to
+// 0.0002 mm -- are destroyed with it. 11 cylinder regions recognised, 1 face shipped.
+//
+// sagitta/R is 0.293 for that culprit and ~3e-5 for a real 144-sided bore.
+//
+// HONEST LIMIT, measured: the ratio does NOT separate harmful patches from harmless
+// ones. L10_nut_housing_normal drops five R=2.0 patches and mechparts/15 six R=10.0
+// patches, and every one is 2 triangles at ratio=0.2929 -- the same 90 deg arc in two
+// facets. This gate is therefore "reject 2-triangle quarter-cylinders", and it is a
+// TRADE: mechparts/15 goes 1 -> 5 cylinders, L10_nut_housing_normal 9 -> 5 matched.
+// It nets positive because the first case is commoner: normal 73.67 -> 74.74
+// (precision 91.93 -> 94.97, built 347 -> 338), fine 50.13 -> 50.51, and closed valid
+// solids rise 200->202 and 74->76.
+//
+// A contagion test -- drop the coarse patch only when an edge-adjacent accepted
+// cylinder is >=10x finer -- was implemented and REFUTED: it fires on neither model,
+// so the coarse patches are not edge-adjacent to the fine bands and the damage travels
+// by some other path. Do not retry that form without first finding the real coupling.
+// A patch this coarse is already being exploded into facets today; refusing it up front
+// costs nothing and stops it taking its neighbours with it.
+// Env-gated; off => no-op.
+bool rejectCoarseArcN21(const MeshView& mv, SegmentWork& work) {
+    const char* e = std::getenv("STL2STEP_N21_SAGRATIO");
+    if (e == nullptr) return true;
+    double maxRatio = std::atof(e);
+    if (!(maxRatio > 0.0)) maxRatio = 0.05;
+    const bool diag = std::getenv("STL2STEP_N21_DIAG") != nullptr;
+    std::vector<Region> keep;
+    keep.reserve(work.accepted.size());
+    size_t dropped = 0;
+    for (Region& r : work.accepted) {
+        if (r.type != SurfType::Cylinder || !(r.radius > 0.0) || !(r.chordSagitta > 0.0)) {
+            keep.push_back(r);
+            continue;
+        }
+        const double ratio = r.chordSagitta / r.radius;
+        if (ratio <= maxRatio) { keep.push_back(r); continue; }
+        if (diag)
+            std::fprintf(stderr,
+                         "N21_COARSE drop R=%.4f sag=%.6f ratio=%.4f nTri=%zu\n",
+                         r.radius, r.chordSagitta, ratio, r.tris.size());
+        r.reject = Reject::ChordConsistency;
+        work.rejected.push_back(r);
+        dropped++;
+    }
+    if (diag)
+        std::fprintf(stderr, "N21_COARSE kept=%zu dropped=%zu maxRatio=%.4f\n",
+                     keep.size(), dropped, maxRatio);
+    work.accepted.swap(keep);
+    return true;
+}
